id=a52sxq_pif_stack
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Play Integrity module stack by default (Zygisk Next 864, TEESimulator 73, PIF 490)
author=CodesRahul96
description=The framework PlayIntegrityHooks (unica/mods/pif, now disabled) no longer reach DEVICE/STRONG on One UI 9 / Android 17. The KernelSU module stack that passes BASIC+DEVICE+STRONG on this phone (2026-10-29: Zygisk Next 1.5.2 864-a4a72ce, TEESimulator v4.0 canary 73-159a65c with one byte changed in its arm64 keymint library so the 144-byte attestation challenge of GMS 26.42.31+ is accepted (challenge limit 128 -> 192; unpatched every check ends in INTERNAL_ERROR -100), Play Integrity Fix v4.9-inject-s 490, meta-overlayfs not needed: none of them mounts files) is shipped as the release zips (sha256 pinned, the one byte documented in PROVENANCE.txt) in /system/etc/k4/gmscompat (root only) with the configs that passed, and installed through ksud (ksud module install) by /system/bin/k4-gmscompat in KernelSU's domain after the metamodule step of k4_metamodule.rc. The Settings "Play Integrity Fix" switch (persist.sys.unica.pif, default on) now turns this stack on/off (ksud module enable/disable, from the next boot); a false left by an older build is reset once. Existing configs, keyboxes and modules the user installed are never touched; a module the user removes is not installed again until the switch is turned off and on. The keybox is not in the public repository: the build ships $K4_PIF_KEYBOX (default /mnt/B1/OneUi9/keybox/keybox.xml) when it exists. Result in sys.k4.gmscompat, log /data/adb/.k4_gmscompat.log.
